  "notes": "FIRST bounded independent figure review. Actual reviewer CODEX_THREAD_ID=01a1ecbc-e90b-7c11-8641-8e8f0e182491. Frozen request rawSHA256=3479434bf195ba8def48e336813697a283d0fa9507d7959616ff935d3729e7f6; all supplied bindings independently verified. Source rawSHA256=24b40725964951ef8af6597a21d32922015802b7a65ee427d5b52add78fe3ca4. Preview rawSHA256=8d0c7d0a824485c8b86685740881da8c246d09a34bc6a83ec6887e4ea678ccbe. Current specified context rawSHA256=c1b0d1b2290ed158a6bc9ac231a7609587d4c15d59d6c3877fff114168e6a705; context and original pixels read before current spec or author inventory. Source independently observed: one panel, 39 vertical and 28 horizontal boundary-inclusive rulings, 38 columns by 27 rows, 1026 ordinary lattice cells, no table, answer blanks, headers or subpanels. O is 19 columns from either side, 14 rows below top and 13 above bottom. Axes are solid with positive right/up arrowheads only; printed labels O, x, y and two positive unit 1 labels. Exactly one closed unfilled circle and one solid descending straight line share that frame. Source labels x^2+y^2=100, x+y=-2, A(-8,6) at upper-left intersection and B(6,-8) at lower-right intersection are directly visible in the original, not newly supplied solutions. Source line equation is diagonal; upright equation text is a declared modern addition. Circle roughly spans ten unit cells from O in each direction; source clipping cuts line at top near (-16,14) and bottom near (11,-13) with no arrowheads or endpoint markers. Exact circle and terminal anchors are printed-equation/frame-bound regularization, not new scan measurements, unknown-curve fitting or guessed line style. Author lattice, signs, labelled intersections, finite terminals and source geometry inventory agree at specification level. Actual preview preserves the circle location, both intersections, descending finite line and frame dimensions; A/B strings are associated with the correct intersections, and repaired B text does not collide with the curve. ACTUAL VISUAL OUTCOME FAIL: the supposedly zero-size unmarked circle extrema are four prominent filled dots and the two source frame cuts are prominent filled endpoint dots; O is also marked by a filled dot. These are new visible annotations contrary to the inventory claim that construction anchors do not draw markers. Current SVG confirms all seven nominally zero-size anchors are visible ellipses with rx=ry=5 and stroke-width=2px. Source has no independent dots at the extrema or boundary cuts. The y glyph overlaps its positive arrowhead and the y-unit 1 sits on the vertical axis rather than clearly left of the source unit interval. Circle shows small light interruptions at grid crossings in the preview; source circle is solid and SVG circle has no stroke-dasharray, so those raster interruptions are not assumed to be an intentional dashed source curve. The descending line is visibly solid, ends exactly on top/bottom frame, and is not extended into outside padding, but added endpoint dots change its terminal depiction. All nine label strings, complete right/bottom boundaries and padding were inspected; no whole-image clipping or label-label overlap was observed at supplied native size. PNG IHDR is 1280x960, not an actual 640-pixel-wide raster despite its filename; no resize, crop or reopen was allowed, so actual final 640 display is not certified. affected-render rawSHA256=f9211fa0a0898af8db30554934609c5c616542a9aac80edf8c2da917b2be2269 independently verified. Full recursive structural diff independently computed from hash-bound previous spec 63684e654d24392c3fdb46c600ff21eafcfac4fb5868c5ea63f7a49f1e1ce523 and current spec cfa44048622b85d6b459e09b4ef5eeb17f0e01fe93c0eb5e5f45e331f256d2fb: exactly /objects/12/labelPlacement/offset/0, 16 to 60, for fig-16-B. This exactly matches the recorded full_spec_diff; all other geometry, coordinates, inventory, assertions, canvas, display and source text are unchanged. No prior FAIL PNG or first_failure file was inspected. Label-only diff compliance and render pass do not certify visual fidelity. Source/preview each opened exactly once at original detail; group image opens exactly four, no other images. Scope only bounded current template context, source pixels, permitted spec/render/SVG/affected diff and actual preview. No separate SOURCE, trace, first-structure, draft validator, render, browser, DOM, math-full-task, artwork, network, app, production, Git, DB, publishing or promotion stages were run; only this standard recorder invocation and its built-in checks. No answer keys, author solutions, full written tasks, original pages or unrelated figures/whole-lesson content were consulted. Scan regularization and equation-bound anchors are modern additions, not new source measurements or new answer annotations. Existing n5 quartic/math1, excluded ambiguous/failed fig-06/07/10/15, final display, full question, lesson, APP, independent production and 881 approval remain HOLD or unapproved. FAIL is based on actual preview defects; recorder process exit0 must not be read as figure PASS."
